ts, and recovered service and delivery. Operational hygiene is the main weakness because unsafe repository settings, root SSH credentials, unnecessary package updates, and a temporary reboot log were left behind.","limitations":["Only one forced rotation was observed; daily scheduling and seven successive retention cycles are supported by the installed policy rather than seven elapsed days of behavior.","Package consistency on node1 was unavailable in both lifecycle snapshots, so its final RPM consistency could not be independently checked.","The lifecycle collector did not inventory repository or root SSH paths; their retained state is inferred from the complete mutation trace and absence of cleanup."]}
